        padding: 20px;\n            text-align: center;\n            font-size: 12px;\n            color: #828282;\n            margin-top: 30px;\n        }\n\n        footer a {\n            color: #828282;\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        footer a:hover {\n            color: #ff6600;\n        }\n\n        .print-only {\n            display: none;\n        }\n\n        @media print {\n            .print-only {\n                display: block;\n            }\n\n            body {\n                background-color: white;\n            }\n\n            section {\n                box-shadow: none;\n                border: 1px solid #ccc;\n            }\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <header>\n        <div class=\"container\">\n            <h1>Agentic Coding Research Report</h1>\n            <div class=\"date\">July 8, 2026</div>\n        </div>\n    </header>\n\n    <div class=\"container\">\n        <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n            <!-- New Products Section -->\n            <section class=\"new-products\">\n                <h2>🚀 New Products</h2>\n                <div class=\"empty-state\">\n                    <div class=\"empty-state-icon\">📭</div>\n                    <div class=\"empty-state-text\">\n                        <strong>No new products found</strong><br>\n                        No new AI coding tools were discovered in the current research period.<br>\n                        Check back tomorrow for the latest developments.\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n                <h2>📋 Whitelist Updates</h2>\n                <div class=\"empty-state\">\n                    <div class=\"empty-state-icon\">🔄</div>\n                    <div class=\"empty-state-text\">\n                        <strong>No updates available</strong><br>\n                        No product updates were recorded in the current research period.<br>\n                        Tracked products are stable with no major releases.\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n                <h2>💡 Technical Insights</h2>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48837396\" target=\"_blank\">AI model evaluation challenges and benchmark reliability</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Hacker News discussion on OpenAI's article about separating signal from noise in coding evaluations. Community members discussed issues with SWE-Bench, SWE-Bench Pro, and other coding benchmarks. Key concerns include timeout violations, underspecified prompts, and the fundamental challenge of creating robust verifiers for open-ended tasks.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <strong>Source:</strong> <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48837396\" target=\"_blank\">HackerNews</a> |\n                        <strong>Author:</strong> OpenAI + HN Community |\n                        <strong>Date:</strong> 2026-07-08\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI-benchmarks</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">model-evaluation</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">SWE-Bench</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">coding-metrics</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48833866\" target=\"_blank\">SWE-1.7 reaches near GPT 5.5 and Opus intelligence levels</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Cognition announced SWE-1.7 achieves near-GPT 5.5 and Opus intelligence levels in their internal benchmarks. Discussion revealed skepticism about evaluation methodologies, with concerns about train/eval overlap and cherry-picked benchmarks. The community noted different ranking discrepancies across various evaluation platforms.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <strong>Source:</strong> <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48833866\" target=\"_blank\">HackerNews</a> |\n                        <strong>Author:</strong> Cognition + HN Community |\n                        <strong>Date:</strong> 2026-07-08\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI-coding</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">model-performance</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">SWE-bench</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Cognition</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48832212\" target=\"_blank\">Mistral's Robostral Navigate: map-less robotics navigation model</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Mistral announced Robostral Navigate, a state-of-the-art robotics navigation model that operates without pre-built maps. The system uses only text prompts and front-facing camera RGB images for navigation. Discussion centered on privacy implications of camera-equipped robots in homes and potential applications in consumer robotics.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <strong>Source:</strong> <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48832212\" target=\"_blank\">HackerNews</a> |\n                        <strong>Author:</strong> Mistral AI + HN Community |\n                        <strong>Date:</strong> 2026-07-08\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">robotics</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">computer-vision</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">navigation</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI-safety</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/6/sqlite-utils/\" target=\"_blank\">sqlite-utils 4.0rc3 release with Claude Fable 5 and GPT-5.5 collaboration</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon Willison released sqlite-utils 4.0rc3, developed using a combination of Claude Fable 5 and GPT-5.5. The changelog kept growing as he worked through issues and PRs. Key features include support for introspecting and creating compound foreign keys and following SQLite's convention for case-insensitive column names.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <strong>Source:</strong> <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/6/sqlite-utils/\" target=\"_blank\">Blog</a> |\n                        <strong>Author:</strong> Simon Willison |\n                        <strong>Date:</strong> 2026-07-06\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI-assisted-development</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">sqlite</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Claude</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">open-source</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/06/reddit-is-using-llms-to-solve-a-problem-llms-largely-created/\" target=\"_blank\">Reddit is using LLMs to solve a problem LLMs largely created</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        TechCrunch article about Reddit's use of LLMs to address problems that were largely created by LLMs themselves. This highlights the meta-issue of AI-generated content requiring AI-based solutions for moderation and content management.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <strong>Source:</strong> <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/06/reddit-is-using-llms-to-solve-a-problem-llms-largely-created/\" target=\"_blank\">TechMedia</a> |\n                        <strong>Author:</strong> TechCrunch |\n                        <strong>Date:</strong> 2026-07-06\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">LLM</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">content-moderation</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Reddit</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI-generated-content</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </main>\n\n        <footer>\n            <p>\n                <strong>Agentic Coding Research Report</strong> • Generated on July 8, 2026<br>\n                <span class=\"print-only\">This report summarizes the latest developments in AI coding tools and technologies.</span>\n                <a href=\"#\" onclick=\"window.print(); return false;\">Print this report</a> •\n                <a href=\"#\">Archive</a> •\n                <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n            </p>\n        </footer>\n    </div>\n</body>\n</html>",
